    "wikitext": "{{Short description|none}}\n{{Multiple issues|\n{{Full citations needed|date=March 2019}}\n{{circular|date=November 2017}}\n{{more citations needed|date=August 2020}}\n{{Update|reason=The Pew Research Center has just published its new worldwide data for 2020, and revised those for 2010. This article should be entirely updated accordingly: https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2025/06/09/how-the-global-religious-landscape-changed-from-2010-to-2020/ ; https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/feature/religious-composition-by-country-2010-2020/|date=June 2025}}\n}}\n{{Use dmy dates|date=October 2023}}\n{{Use Oxford spelling|date=November 2017}}\n\n[[File:Prevailing religious population by country percentage.svg|thumb|300x300px|Map of prevailing religion by country]]\n[[File:Religion in the world.PNG|thumb|300x300px|Map of relative importance of religion by country, based on a 2006–2008 worldwide survey by Gallup]]\n[[File:State Religions.svg|thumb|Countries with a [[state religion]]:\n{| width=\"100%\"\n|-\n| valign=\"top\" |\n{{legend|#1600FF|[[Christianity]] (unspecified)}}\n{{legend|#062A87|[[Protestantism]]}}\n{{legend|#0774F1|[[Eastern Orthodoxy]]}}\n{{legend|#04E3F1|[[Catholicism]]}}\n| valign=\"top\" |\n{{legend|#158706|[[Islam]] (unspecified)}}\n{{legend|#0F5D05|[[Sunni Islam]]}}\n{{legend|#2FEB16|[[Shi'a Islam]]}}\n| valign=\"top\" |\n{{legend|#EBCF16|[[Theravada|Theravada Buddhism]]}}\n{{legend|#D4AA00|[[Vajrayana|Vajrayana Buddhism]]}}\n|}\n|300x300px]]\n{{Religions by country sidebar}}\n\nThis is an overview of religion by country or territory in 2020 according to a 2025\n[[Pew Research Center]] report.<ref name=pewResearch>{{citation |author= Conrad Hackett, Marcin Stonawski, Yunping Tong, Stephanie Kramer, Anne Shi and Dalia Fahmy|date=June 2025 |title=How the Global Religious Landscape Changed From 2010 to 2020|publisher=Pew Research Center |url=https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2025/06/09/how-the-global-religious-landscape-changed-from-2010-to-2020/ |access-date=13 October 2025}}</ref> The article Religious information by country gives information from [[The World Factbook]] of the [[Central Intelligence Agency|CIA]] and the [[United States Department of State|U.S. Department of State]].\n\n==World==\n{| class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align:right\"\n|+\n!Religion\n!Population\n!Percentage\n|-\n![[Christianity]]\n|2,268,860,000\n|28.8%\n|-\n![[Islam]]\n|2,022,590,000\n|25.6%\n|-\n![[Hinduism]]\n|1,177,860,000\n|14.9%\n|-\n![[Buddhism]]\n|624,190,000\n|6.6%\n|-\n![[Judaism]]\n|14,780,000\n|0.2%\n|-\n!World\n!5,808,280,000\n!73.6%\n|}\nAccording to Pew's 2025 data, around 73.6% of the world adheres to at least one of the five major world religions, while the remaining 26.4% is [[Irreligion|religiously unaffiliated]] or practicing [[Folk religion|folk traditions]], represented by 1,908,590,000 being unaffiliated at 24.2%, and 170,000,000 participating in other practices having a share of 2.2%.<ref name=\"pewResearch\" />\n\n== Africa ==\n<div>{{Religions by country table Africa}}</div>\n\n== Americas ==\n<div>{{Religions by country table Americas}}</div>\n\n== Asia ==\n<div>{{Religions by country table Asia }}</div>\n\n== Europe ==\n<div>{{Religions by country table Europe}}</div>\n\n== Oceania ==\n<div>{{Religions by country table Oceania }}\n\n== 2020 Pew Research World Religious Landscape ==\nTable shows the religious makeup of 201 countries and territories <ref>{{Cite web |last=Zanetti |first=Conrad Hackett, Marcin Stonawski, Yunping Tong, Stephanie Kramer, Anne Shi and Nick |date=2025-06-09 |title=Religious Composition by Country, 2010-2020 |url=https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/feature/religious-composition-by-country-2010-2020/ |access-date=2025-08-08 |website=Pew Research Center |language=en-US}}</ref>\n{| class=\"wikitable sortable\"\n!Country\n!Christians\n!Muslims\n!Unaffiliated\n!Hindus\n!Buddhists\n!Other religions\n!Jews\n!Total\n|-\n|World\n|2,268,860,000\n|2,022,590,000\n|1,905,360,0